# --- Text files: force LF (repo convention, see rustfmt.toml newline_style) ---
# Without this rule, core.autocrlf=true (system default on Windows) checks out CRLF
# into the worktree, which conflicts with rustfmt newline_style=Unix and makes
# .githooks/pre-commit "cargo fmt --check" fail on every commit.
# Binary/asset types above are already marked -text by the LFS rules.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Binary/asset types: keep them out of text normalization (LFS rules above set -text;
# this block restores -text AFTER the global '* text=auto' rule, whose later position
# in the file would otherwise override it and let git normalize LFS content).
